ard to control.\n\nOK proceed: two traces with busybox md5sum. Also should I first check fw_list_traces to see prior runs? Not required. Let me fire the first trace now, then poll.\n\nActually, let me reconsider applet to get a meaningful diff. \"md5sum\" — computing hash over \"hello\" vs empty file involves the same functions but with different loop counts; per-function coverage diff likely empty. Honest report allows empty diff. But the user says \"空差分也要如实写\" — so empty diff is acceptable to report. Good.\n\nBut maybe better to choose an applet with branchy parse: \"pk\" or \"dpkg\" decompression: busybox `tar` (applet \"tar\") with payload being a tar archive header — parse branches. Complex. Or \"ash\"? That's a shell — reads script from stdin; parses with branching. argv0=\"sh\", payload=\"echo hello\". Shell parsing would show a good diff vs empty input (empty input exits immediately, \"echo hello\" parses commands","stream":true,"block":0}

