data: {"seq":83,"ts":"2026-08-23T08:39:43.822Z","text":"Trace 1 failed: `QemuError: empty coverage log (target rc=2); sh: 1: cannot open /tmp/fwgraph-stdin: No such file`. So the stdin via mechanism dropped the file at /tmp/fwgraph-stdin, but busybox sh on this firmware — when the applet is \"sh\" invoked non-interactively without a script or -c, ash reads from stdin which was redirected to /tmp/fwgraph-stdin, but the file doesn't exist? Interesting: the harness writes stdin to /tmp/fwgraph-stdin inside the guest and redirects fd0. But the error says \"cannot open /tmp/fwgraph-stdin: No such file\" — hmm, that's the shell reporting an error when opening... Actually ash applet with no argv: when stdin is not a tty, ash reads commands from stdin. The message suggests the harness ran busybox sh with stdin redirected from a file that was never created, or the file path is seen differently.\n\nThis looks like a platform quirk: maybe stdin via","stream":true,"block":0}

