LF\" I'd prefer something like busybox `unzip -l /tmp/poc.bin` (structured file parser) or `tar -t -f`. A zip parser: busybox unzip with a small crafted zip would give interesting coverage diff. But crafting zip hex is more work;to keep capability acceptance simple, md5sum file read is fine, and I can report both honestly. Actually let me pick something with actual parsing to make the diff meaningful: `busybox unzip -l /tmp/poc.bin` needs valid zip. Too much.\n\nAlternative richer stdin parser: busybox applet `base64`? decodes stdin... `base64` vs `base64 -d`. Parsing base64 input \"aGVsbG8=\" — base64 decode from stdin. Function-wise, decode path chosen. Hmm binary/ASCII. md5sum simpler.\n\nBetter idea: use `od`/`hexdump`? Reads stdin, parses. Eh.\n\nI'll go:\n- Trace 1: argv0=\"md5sum\", stdin payload \"hello\\n\"? payload bytes 10 - \"echo hello\" was 10. Use payload \"hello\".\n- Trace 2: argv0=\"md5sum\", argv=[\"/tmp/poc.bin\"], input_path=/tmp/poc.bin, payload_hex hex of \"hello\" (68656c6c6f).\n\nPoll both. If still empty diffs, report honestly.\n\nNote: baseline for md5sum with empty stdin: md5sum of empty input still runs hashing code path with 0 bytes. Trigger \"hello\": same functions, different loop. diff.function_count likely 0 (empty diff). That's the honest result. \n\nWait — the user explicitly warns \"空差分也要如实写\" so they anticipate empties. Good.\n\nBut maybe I can pick an applet where input genuinely changes control flow: `uudecode`? `bunzip2`? `gzip -d`? For gunzip determinism: busybox gunzip applet with stdin payload of random bytes → \"invalid gzip magic\" error path quickly; baseline empty stdin → gunzip reads block 0, finds EOF → different branch? Probably similar functions but maybe different branches. Eh.\n\nActually `cpio`/`tar`? busybox `tar -t` reading a header from stdin... \n\nHonestly md5sum is the safe deterministic choice; the point is capability demonstration, not vuln. Go.\n\nAlso note checksec from trace 1's binary: canary false, nx false, pie false, relro none — relevant for future finding context but no record_finding now.\n\nFire both retries.","stream":true,"block":0}

