ght be because input_path drop failed or the file write step is broken for pure-stdin payloads (payload without input_path). Notice: in c30ceb41dcef (which has input_path=/tmp/poc.bin AND payload_hex), still running — maybe THAT one works because with input_path set, the file-drop works and the stdin redirection also works?\n\nBut the error for eb2d054e452a says cannot open /tmp/fwgraph-stdin — that's the stdin file, not /tmp/poc.bin.\n\nHmm wait, actually maybe the flow is: via=stdin → harness writes payload to guest /tmp/fwgraph-stdin (must exist) and invokes busybox as `sh` reading that file? But then argv0 should have been honored... The error would be from qemu prefix like `-0 md5sum`? No, ash error prefix is the applet name \"sh\".\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the harness ignores argv0 entirely and always appends /tmp/fwgraph-stdin as a script when via=stdin, invoking `busybox sh /tmp/fwgraph-stdin`? Then applet is sh regardless. That matches: error \"sh: 1: cannot open /tmp/fwgraph-stdin\". So for via=stdin, the harness runs the busybox with arg [sh, /tmp/fwgraph-stdin]? But then argv field we set would conflict... c30ceb41dcef has argv=[\"/tmp/poc.bin\"] and is","stream":true,"block":0}

