ser cant' easily pipe? Actually qemu-user CAN pipe host stdin directly. The traces failing suggest the harness uses a guest-side file for stdin (dropped from host), and that drop is broken for pure-stdin trace runs (no input_path). Possibly a platform bug: pure via=stdin payload isn't materialized. But user says don't claim platform capability missing — but we should report honestly what happened. Note: the user said \"禁止说缺少平台能力\" — forbid claiming missing platform capabilities as an excuse without evidence. But here we have concrete trace evidence: file-input path works, pure-stdin path errors with a real harness error (rc=2). That's factual reporting, not excuse-making — the user explicitly said \"空差分也要如实写\" i.e., honest reporting.\n\nLet me try ONE more pure-stdin variant with a non-busybox binary to see if pure stdin works at all. Which ELF reads stdin? A standalone one that parses: hmm. In this firmware, candidates: \n- `usr/bin/dropbearkey`? no.\n- `bin/arpping`? no.\n- `usr/sbin/dhcp6c`? network.\n- `ntfs-3g`? device.\n- What about a binary that by default reads a FILE (config) — that's the input_path case which already works.\n\nHonestly the c30ceb41dcef trace already satisfies step 4 (input_path=/tmp/poc.bin + payload_hex → ok_empty_diff). For step 3 (via=stdin pure), I have two failed attempts with trace_id+status recorded. To be thorough, let me try one more: via=stdin with busybox but","stream":true,"block":0}

