data: {"seq":264,"ts":"2026-08-23T08:40:58.396Z","text":"c95138e9a87a also failed with the same error: `sh: 1: cannot open /tmp/fwgraph-stdin: No such file`, despite argv=[\"md5sum\"]. So the via=stdin channel in this platform trace harness materializes payload to /tmp/fwgraph-stdin and launches the binary with applet `sh` + that path (busybox-special handling), and the file-drop fails → rc=2, empty coverage.\n\nConclusion: On this platform, the qemu-user trace harness's pure via=stdin channel for busybox is non-functional (file never materialized), while the file-input channel (input_path) works fully and produced a real 45-function diff. argv0 forging is not applied by the qemu exec path (usage screen proved it), so busybox multicall selection must go through argv, which works via input_path channel (argv=[\"/tmp/poc.bin\"] with argv0=sh actually ran `sh /tmp/poc.bin` since argv0 was honored in the trace harness? Wait — for a432876827e2, argv0=\"sh\" argv=[\"/tmp/poc.bin\"], and result shows functions 79 with vfork/execve → sh ran /tmp/poc.bin as script. For c30ceb41dcef, argv0=\"md5sum\" argv=[\"/tmp/poc.bin\"] → 26 funcs, no exec, and empty diff; suspicious md5sum didn't print hash but that's fine — 26 funcs consistent with md5sum reading 5-byte file; diff 0 because baseline also runs md5sum on empty? trigger_result kind input_path sent 5. Empty diff is honest: md5sum's code path identical regardless of content length 0 vs 5 (same functions, different loop iterations).)\n\nHmm wait, so argv0 IS honored in the trace harness (a432876827e2 ran as sh successfully, c30ceb41dcef as md5sum) but NOT in fw_qemu_exec. OK.\n\nSo final capability acceptance summary:\n\n1) ELF selected: busybox (md5 aa3d98e20b0f5904d08b51eed6a9536a, bin/busybox, MIPS32be) — reads stdin/file via sh script & md5sum. (No :80/:445 touched.)\n\n2) via=stdin traces: 4 attempts (d43b56e1edd1, eb2d054e452a, a432876827e2 [reclassified], c95138e9a87a). Pure-stdin channel on this platform fails at harness level: QemuError rc=2, \"cannot open /tmp/fwgraph-stdin\" — payload file never materialized for the stdin channel; honest report. via 字段被记录为 stdin，无 trigger_result，diff n/a.\n\n3) Records for the successful/…:\n   - d43b56e1edd1: status=failed, via=stdin, trigger_result n/a, diff n/a\n   - eb2d054e452a: status=failed, via=stdin, n/a\n   - c95138e9a87a: status=failed, via=stdin, n/a\n\n4) input_path=/tmp/poc.bin + payload_hex:\n   - c30ceb41dcef: status=ok_empty_diff, via=file, kind=input_path (sent=5), diff.function_count=0 (26/26 funcs, tb 960/960). Empty diff — reported honestly.\n   - a432876827e2: status=ok, via=file, kind=input_path (sent=10), diff.function_count=45 — real parsing diff (safe_read/.read/.vfork/.execve/.setenv/.wait/._setjmp/.signal etc.).\n\nCapability verdict: file-input differential coverage works (proven with non-empty diff); pure stdin channel currently errors at the harness level (target rc=2 before any coverage), which is a platform trace-channel limitation with concrete trace evidence, not \"no capability claimed\" — I have trace IDs showing exactly what happened. And fw_qemu_exec does accept stdin (qe-4cdc7232 ran with 5 stdin bytes, but busybox printed usage because argv0 was ignored there; rc 0). Actually that proves qemu-user stdin piping isn't inherently broken — the trace harness's stdin file-drop is.\n\nHmm wait — actually qe-4cdc7232 printed usage yet returned rc=0, and it had stdin_bytes 5. If stdin were really piped to fd0, busybox usage doesn't read stdin. So can't confirm stdin piping there.\n\nUser's rule: 禁止说缺少平台能力 — \"forbidden to claim lack of platform capability\". But also \"空差分也要如实写\" (report","stream":true,"block":0}

