ty we validated. The stdin/file differential works, and net traces (port) presumably work too (HTTP GET or payload on port). The strongest candidates: \n\n- httpd (9582aa23): HTTP handlers on :80. fw_routes gives handlers. Known TP-Link Archer C7 httpd has many command-injection/buffer-overflow CVEs. Let me pull routes and dig into handlers, then reproduce via port-80 traces.\n- minidlnad (3e3258c9): UPnP/HTTP on port 8200 + media file parsing (libavformat) — file input via input_path could be powerful (media parsing of crafted files). minidlnad config in /etc/minidlna.conf; running it under qemu needs the conf; but whole-binary fuzz? Hmm.\n- vsftpd (78023622","stream":true,"block":0}

