data: {"seq":377,"ts":"2026-08-23T09:09:57.726Z","text":"sub_40F168: builds \"echo \\\"====>>>>%s\\\" > /dev/ttyS0\" and calls sub_40F0F8 → system(). So this is the *debug logging* path: dprintf → echo to serial console. The \"%s\" content = log message (dprintf's message, built with snprintf from constants mostly). Not","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":378,"ts":"2026-08-23T09:09:58.107Z","text":"sub_40F168: builds \"echo \\\"====>>>>%s\\\" > /dev/ttyS0\" and calls sub_40F0F8 → system(). So this is the *debug logging* path: dprintf → echo to serial console. The \"%s\" content = log message (dprintf's message, built with snprintf from constants mostly). Not a cmdi from network. So dhcp6s P0 is definitively a debug-log combo, not attacker-controllable format. Drop dhcp6s.\n\nNow read rcS to see service launch lines (httpd argv, minidlnad argv, dhcp6s argv) to build","stream":true,"block":0}

