w area. Is dnsproxy stdin/testable? It reads from socket. Hmm.\n\nOK here's the thing — every juicy parser here is a network daemon, and our net trace works only for TCP (httpd empty). UDP daemons (dhcp6s UDP 547, dnsproxy UDP 53, minidlnad UDP 1900) can't be driven by via=net (it does TCP connect + payload). \n\nBUT: the identification's AS-004 said dhcp6s is \"tcp\"! Because the ctl channel is TCP. And /etc/dhcp6sctlkey exists. The **dhcp6s ctl TCP channel** IS reachable via via=net! What's the ctl port? -p option default: off_43C074. KAME dhcp6s default ctlport = DHCP6CTL_PORT = 0x0691? Actually 547? In KAME, DHCP6CTL_PORT is 6969? Let me check: KAME dhcp6ctl uses port 5555? I recall dhcp6ctl_port default 5555 in some; or","stream":true,"block":0}

