data: {"seq":501,"ts":"2026-08-23T09:10:47.614Z","text":"sub_40D1FC analysis (UPnP HTTP request line parser):\n\n```\nv5 = *(a1+32) // request buffer\n// 1st token (method): copy up to 15 bytes into v7[16] — bounded ok\n// skip spaces; if starts with \"http://\", advance to next '/'\n// 2nd token (URL): copy up to 511 into v8[500]?? wait v8[7]!! \n```\n\nLook: `char v8[7];` — BUT `for (i=0; i<511 && *v5!=32 && *v5!=13; ++i) v8[i] = *v5++;` copies UP TO 511 bytes into v8 which is declared as 7 bytes! That's the classic **stack buffer overflow in upnphttp.c","stream":true,"block":0}

