what it needs (args, web root) — via fw_get_function_source on httpd main. Find httpd main addr: search? httpd has 4882 funcs. Use identification IN-014? main addr unknown. Use fw_search(\"main\") in job? pattern \"httpd\"? Let me fw_search pattern \"^main$\" limit... too broad. \n\nAlternative: the wmnet* functions (wmnetTcpRead etc.) are the accept/read layer; sub_420B48 reads/writes. The actual HTTP request parsing is likely httpMimeParse (0x444940) — \"HTTP mime parse\" (headers) — and httpLineUnescape. Let me read httpMimeParse full + httpLineUnescape + httpBase64decode (0x42faf4) — normalizers typically have the strcpy bugs.\n\nGiven budget, let me focus: read httpMimeParse (0x444940) full and httpLineUnescape (0x432fc0) full. If either copies attacker header data into fixed buffer with no bound → recordable after net-trace verification.\n\nThen run a port-80 trace with a crafted","stream":true,"block":0}

