h`/ash — known vulns? Let me check msh: BusyBox 1.01's \"msh\" applet (it's listed!). But sh is ash. Fun fact: BusyBox 1.01 ash had CVE-2006-1056? no. Hmm.\n\nLet me change tactics completely: instead of trying to find a NEW bug, reuse the platform's FAMOUS one: **the uclited/ipcserver \"TP-Link CLI\"**? Unknown protocols.\n\nActually — WAIT. Let me reconsider **httpd**. The famous Archer C7 CVE-2017-13772: \"TP-Link Archer C7 httpd: 'Ping Test' command injection via pingAddr\" — standard \"Diag\" cgi. And CVEs in \"cgi\" handlers (userRpm). The httpd parses POST forms and runs commands (ping/nslookup) with injected shell metachars. Our dynamic tool CAN hit :80 via net trace but yielded empty diff. The problem might be the trace harness","stream":true,"block":0}

