vation; it can crash-check via the harness?** No — fw_get_trace trigger_result won't crash a daemon typically (it sends one request). fw_qemu_exec could run dropbear and... it needs a client.\n\nOK. Let me accept: this session's successful dynamic surface is stdin/file. The most promising REAL bug I've seen statically that is ALSO dynamically driveable via file:\n\n**minidlnad media parsing** — but minidlnad won't run (needs config/db, and it's a daemon binding ports — actually if it CAN run under qemu: it binds 8200 & 1900; and scans media dirs. If config absent → default options? sub_405D5C reads options file /etc/minidlna.conf; if missing → defaults? It might default to no media dirs and just serve UPnP XML (functional but no media). Then HTTP traces to :8200 would work → /rootDesc.xml, /MediaItems/... but no DB → empty lists. The thumbnail handlers need DB rows → 404. So no file parsing reachable without media db. BUT we could run minidlnad and inject a sqlite DB? Too much.\n\n**Decision**: pivot to fuzzing a busybox msh/sh? Weak.\n\nActually, let me revisit identification for **IN-001 athadhoc / IN-002 bpalogin / IN-005 dnsproxy / IN-003 dhcp6c**: dhcp6c parses DHCPv6 replies — network. All UDP clients/daemons.\n\nAlright — pragmatic finale: Given everything, THE strongest","stream":true,"block":0}

