data: {"seq":710,"ts":"2026-08-23T09:13:19.327Z","text":"Process_upnphttp: buffer is realloc'd to hold everything; sub_40C538 finds \"\\r\\n\\r\\n\" end of headers → a1+44 = header-end offset, a1+40 = content-length (from header). Then sub_40D1FC runs when enough data arrived (a1+36 - a1+44 >= a1+40), or immediately after first recv with the full thing (state0 path).\n\nsub_40D1FC chunked decode:\n- (a1+116)&0x100 → chunked. Then:\n```\nv3 = (a1+32) + (a1+44)  // start of body\ndest = v3\nloop:\n  (a1+112) = strtol(nptr, &src, 16)  // nptr starts at body start\n  if (!chunklen || src==nptr) break\n  skip to CRLF; src = src+2\n  memmove(dest, src, chunklen)\n  dest += chunklen\n  nptr = src + chunklen   // next chunk header candidate\n(a1+40) = dest - v3\n(a1+36) = dest - (a1+32)\n```\nThe memmove copies from src onward WITH","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":711,"ts":"2026-08-23T09:13:19.677Z","text":"Process_upnphttp: buffer is realloc'd to hold everything; sub_40C538 finds \"\\r\\n\\r\\n\" end of headers → a1+44 = header-end offset, a1+40 = content-length (from header). Then sub_40D1FC runs when enough data arrived (a1+36 - a1+44 >= a1+40), or immediately after first recv with the full thing (state0 path).\n\nsub_40D1FC chunked decode:\n- (a1+116)&0x100 → chunked. Then:\n```\nv3 = (a1+32) + (a1+44)  // start of body\ndest = v3\nloop:\n  (a1+112) = strtol(nptr, &src, 16)  // nptr starts at body start\n  if (!chunklen || src==nptr) break\n  skip to CRLF; src = src+2\n  memmove(dest, src, chunklen)\n  dest += chunklen\n  nptr = src + chunklen   // next chunk header candidate\n(a1+40) = dest - v3\n(a1+36) = dest - (a1+32)\n```\nThe memmove copies from src onward WITHIN the original buffer — since dest ≤ src always (dest starts at body, src starts after first chunk header), this is in-place left","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":712,"ts":"2026-08-23T09:13:20.124Z","text":"Process_upnphttp: buffer is realloc'd to hold everything; sub_40C538 finds \"\\r\\n\\r\\n\" end of headers → a1+44 = header-end offset, a1+40 = content-length (from header). Then sub_40D1FC runs when enough data arrived (a1+36 - a1+44 >= a1+40), or immediately after first recv with the full thing (state0 path).\n\nsub_40D1FC chunked decode:\n- (a1+116)&0x100 → chunked. Then:\n```\nv3 = (a1+32) + (a1+44)  // start of body\ndest = v3\nloop:\n  (a1+112) = strtol(nptr, &src, 16)  // nptr starts at body start\n  if (!chunklen || src==nptr) break\n  skip to CRLF; src = src+2\n  memmove(dest, src, chunklen)\n  dest += chunklen\n  nptr = src + chunklen   // next chunk header candidate\n(a1+40) = dest - v3\n(a1+36) = dest - (a1+32)\n```\nThe memmove copies from src onward WITHIN the original buffer — since dest ≤ src always (dest starts at body, src starts after first chunk header), this is in-place left-shift. dest advances by chunklen each time. The TOTAL copied = sum of chunklen ≤ declared chunk sizes. If the attacker declares a huge chunklen (strtol 16 hex → up to ~2^31), memmove(dest, src, 0x7","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":713,"ts":"2026-08-23T09:13:20.484Z","text":"Process_upnphttp: buffer is realloc'd to hold everything; sub_40C538 finds \"\\r\\n\\r\\n\" end of headers → a1+44 = header-end offset, a1+40 = content-length (from header). Then sub_40D1FC runs when enough data arrived (a1+36 - a1+44 >= a1+40), or immediately after first recv with the full thing (state0 path).\n\nsub_40D1FC chunked decode:\n- (a1+116)&0x100 → chunked. Then:\n```\nv3 = (a1+32) + (a1+44)  // start of body\ndest = v3\nloop:\n  (a1+112) = strtol(nptr, &src, 16)  // nptr starts at body start\n  if (!chunklen || src==nptr) break\n  skip to CRLF; src = src+2\n  memmove(dest, src, chunklen)\n  dest += chunklen\n  nptr = src + chunklen   // next chunk header candidate\n(a1+40) = dest - v3\n(a1+36) = dest - (a1+32)\n```\nThe memmove copies from src onward WITHIN the original buffer — since dest ≤ src always (dest starts at body, src starts after first chunk header), this is in-place left-shift. dest advances by chunklen each time. The TOTAL copied = sum of chunklen ≤ declared chunk sizes. If the attacker declares a huge chunklen (strtol 16 hex → up to ~2^31), memmove(dest, src, 0x7FFFFFFF) — wow, memmove with gigantic length would read src which lies inside the realloc'd buffer of size (a1+36)... memmove copies chunklen bytes from src (within buffer) to dest (within buffer","stream":true,"block":0}

